# requirements/integration/integration.ears
# Integration Architecture v0.4.0 §10 (docs/integration.md). ADR-017 to ADR-022 accepted 2026-10-28;
# each requirement flips to approved in the pull request that lands its behaviour and tests.
capability: Capability-driven integration
owner: integration
requirements:
  - id: INT-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The capability registry shall hold a SourceCapabilityDescriptor with a verification date for every registered source, read from the IVOA registry and VOSI when the source publishes them."
    rationale: "Read, not invent: the registry already describes most sources (ADR-017). A large archive is scanned only over the collections SDP uses, and where its own extent query times out the registry's coverage stands in. Registry queries are plain ADQL (joins, no scalar subqueries) against GAVO's RegTAP host. When the DISTINCT products scan times out, each product type is proven per collection by a TOP 1 probe, a failed probe is an error rather than absence, access is proprietary unless a public product is probed, and instruments and calibration levels stay unpublished (partial, never unsatisfied)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T11]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: INT-002
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a descriptor claims a product type for which no IntegrationConformanceSuite has passed in the current release, then the harness shall remove the claim and fail the release report."
    rationale: "A source cannot advertise a capability its adapter has not proven (ADR-021)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [harness]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-003
    pattern: event
    text: "When a capability match is requested for a field and an evidence requirement, the system shall return every registered source with a per-field reason."
    rationale: "A planner and a reviewer read the same explanation. Every requested constraint is a reported field, one-sided bands and calibration levels included; what a source does not publish is partial, never satisfied. An adapter not yet admitted is partial too: its evidence may feed an exploratory run, and a verdict on it stays refused (INT-016)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-004
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The product envelope shall record each product's cutout support from its DataLink and SODA descriptors or a byte-range probe of its own URL."
    rationale: "Cutouts differ product by product, so support is never assumed per archive. MAST publishes no SODA service for JWST, but its downloads answer HTTP range requests, so an uncompressed FITS image is cut by reading only its headers and the rows the square covers, pixels unchanged. A profile asks for cutouts with cutout_arcsec; the planner then names one field-wide cutout per product, and Retrieve leaves out a product it cannot cut rather than fetching it whole."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T3, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-005
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The kernel shall keep the original bytes of every ingested product as an immutable raw artifact with a SHA-256 of the bytes actually read."
    rationale: "Curation never rewrites the raw file (ADR-018), and a binary curated form is never stamped. A reference product is refused before it is written when it is too large to commit."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T5]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: INT-006
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The product normalizer shall give every product envelope its frame, epoch, time scale, units, calibration level, uncertainty and quality presence, access status, rights, citation and relationships."
    rationale: "Scientific meaning is part of the envelope, not implied. A product that cannot be enveloped (not in the archive's inventory, or unreadable) stays raw evidence and is never curated; envelopes apply only to the missions their dialect reads."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T5s]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-007
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a curated representation would lose an extension, a WCS, an uncertainty array or a quality mask present in the raw product, then the validator shall block curation."
    rationale: "Curation preserves what the science reads."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T5s]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-008
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a product's product_type is preview, thumbnail or auxiliary, then the system shall not curate it as science."
    rationale: "Previews and auxiliaries are never evidence."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T5s]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-009
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The association service shall retain every candidate association with its posterior, prior and evidence, rather than select a nearest neighbour on its own."
    rationale: "Nearest-neighbour matching silently asserts identity (ADR-019). Candidates are selected by true angular separation, so a source near the antipode is never one."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T8]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-010
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The association service shall compare detections at a common epoch, using propagated astrometry with grown covariance."
    rationale: "A 1950s plate and a 2023 detection are compared at one epoch or not at all."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T2]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-011
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If an association is set to accepted without a ledger entry, then the kernel shall refuse the transition."
    rationale: "Identity is a reviewer's signed decision."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-012
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The two association implementations shall agree on the reference fixture within the declared tolerance before either feeds a gate."
    rationale: "Principle 12: anything that issues a probability is implemented twice."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-013
    pattern: event
    text: "When an investigation is planned, the system shall write a content-addressed AcquisitionPlan naming every item, its expected size, its purpose and its access status before any acquisition."
    rationale: "Plans become reproducible evidence (ADR-020). The plan's intent document is its artifact, so its artifact id is its plan id; requirements come from the profile's tests, products from each archive's index over the field, and a requirement no source satisfies is a gap with its reason. The harness re-derives the plan id, the minimum set and the gaps from the candidates the plan records (rederive-plan)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4, harness]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-014
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a plan exceeds the profile's AcquisitionBudget threshold, then the system shall require a signed ledger approval before execution."
    rationale: "Large downloads become signed decisions. The approval is the ledger entry itself, bound to the plan id and the actor; an entry id alone, an entry for another plan or an automatic approval approves nothing above the threshold, and every budget limit is checked, not only bytes. The harness refuses an automatic approval above the threshold and an approval without its ledger entry. A request may tighten the operator's budget but never relax it, and an approval entry must verify against allowed_signers."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4, harness]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-015
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If an acquisition is requested that no approved plan item names, then the executor shall refuse it and record the refusal."
    rationale: "Nothing is downloaded that a hashed plan did not name. The executor's gate refuses every catalogue query and product download no approved item names and records each refusal in PlanExecuted; items the run could not find are listed as unavailable."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-016
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a manifest names an adapter without a passing AdapterCompatibilityRecord for a product type the experiment used, then the platform shall withhold the verdict and block publication."
    rationale: "Admission to a gate is checked, not asserted (ADR-021). It is checked per adapter version, so a record for an older version never admits a newer one, and an input naming only part of adapter, version and product type is unadmitted. A reference record is verified when one named person has checked it against the documentation: SDP is a single-user app (decided 2026-10-29)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, harness]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-017
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The Investigate SourceRegistry shall list only VO services that have a registered SourceCapabilityDescriptor and whose recorded coverage does not exclude the field."
    rationale: "A source is admitted to SDP only with a descriptor (v0.4.0 §2); discovery reads the capability registry rather than every service the IVOA registry knows (D37)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-018
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The capability registry shall keep every descriptor it has registered; a newer descriptor supersedes the current one and no descriptor is edited or deleted."
    rationale: "A plan records the descriptors it was matched against; they must stay readable (ADR-020)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T5]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-019
    pattern: event
    text: "When Retrieve fetches a product from a source with a normaliser, the system shall register the raw bytes with the adapter and product type, store the product's envelope with its validation report, and curate only after the report and the curation check pass."
    rationale: "The envelope is what SDP queries and the report is stored beside the product (v0.4.0 §3, ADR-018); admission needs the adapter on every input (INT-016). A cutout is checked against its own bytes: the inventory's size is the whole file's, which failed every M92 cutout until 2026-10-29."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-020
    pattern: event
    text: "When an investigation profile reads image products, the image-counterpart test shall detect sources on each image, associate them with the field's Gaia sources propagated to the image epoch by both association methods, and flag a Gaia source with no counterpart or one displaced beyond its combined covariance."
    rationale: "The JWST vertical slice adds no science algorithm (v0.4.0 §7): detection is the detector service, association is ADR-019's two methods, and every retained hypothesis, including a blended detection's competing members, reaches the dossier with its posteriors. A profile may first align each image to the propagated Gaia sources (align_wcs), a single shift fitted by the refiner and recorded with the result, because an archived image's absolute astrometry can be off by arcseconds (1.9 arcsec on programme 1334's M92 mosaics, checked live 2026-10-29); a shift moves the frame, so a star displaced from the rest still stands out."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T4]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-021
    pattern: event
    text: "When a product recording is given a size limit above the committed reference-product cap, the system shall write the product only to a folder outside fixtures/, streamed to disk and stopped at the limit."
    rationale: "Full-size JWST mosaics (287 MB for jw01538-o069_t001_nircam_clear-f277w_i2d.fits) are for local testing; they must never be committed by accident, and must not be held in memory or kept in a cassette (#61)."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3]
    status: approved
    traces:
      - "python/tests.archives.test_reference_recording::test_sizes_are_read_like_500mb_or_2gb"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_reference_recording::test_a_bad_size_is_refused_with_an_example"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_reference_recording::test_under_the_cap_the_product_is_fetched_through_the_cassette_transport"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_reference_recording::test_over_the_default_cap_without_the_flag_is_refused"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_reference_recording::test_over_the_cap_with_the_flag_streams_outside_fixtures_and_keeps_no_product_cassette"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_reference_recording::test_a_large_pull_into_fixtures_is_refused_before_anything_is_fetched"
      - "python/tests.archives.test_reference_recording::test_a_stream_that_passes_its_limit_is_stopped_and_removed"
  - id: INT-022
    pattern: event
    text: "When a product is served as a VOTable through DataLink, the envelope validator shall hold its envelope to the same rules as a FITS product's, taking each column's role from its UCD."
    rationale: "Observatory independence (Leigh, 2026-10-29): Gaia DR3 serves epoch photometry and BP/RP spectra as DataLink products rather than TAP tables. The VOTable's tables are read into the structure FITS HDUs give, its TIMESYS states the time scale (TCB for Gaia), and a stat.error or meta.code.status column the file has must be listed in the envelope, as an ERR or DQ extension must. Epoch photometry is calibration level 2 and curates to the canonical lightcurve (G band, photometry and variability rejections dropped, MJD from the barycentric TCB transit time); a mean BP/RP spectrum is level 3 and is read as served."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T3, T4, T5]
    status: approved
    traces: []
  - id: INT-023
    pattern: event
    text: "When a WISE or NEOWISE light curve is fetched from IRSA, the light-curve dialect shall curate its clean W1 exposures into the canonical lightcurve and offer each exposure as an association record at its own epoch with WISE's 6.1-arcsecond resolution."
    rationale: "Time-domain ingestion beyond Gaia (Leigh, 2026-10-29): NEOWISE revisits each star for about a day every six months from 2013 to 2024, a cadence, angular resolution and epoch regime unlike Gaia's or JWST's. A light curve is one cone query on IRSA's per-exposure table (neowiser_p1bs_psd or allwise_p3as_mep) around an AllWISE source, enveloped by the same validator as every other product, with the quality columns the curation reads listed as quality extensions. Curation keeps exposures of a good frame at full image quality, clear of the SAA and the Moon, unblended, and not flagged as an artefact. A WISE beam often holds two Gaia stars; the association service offers them as one blend, and since the flux split in W1 is unknown, the blend's expected position is widened by where between its members the light can fall."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1, T3, T4, T5]
    status: approved
    traces: []
